What is a Collection?
Interview Definition

A Collection is a framework that provides classes and interfaces to store,
manage, and manipulate groups of objects dynamically.

Simple Definition

Collections are smart containers.

They can:

Grow automatically.
Shrink automatically.
Insert elements easily.
Delete elements easily.
Search efficiently (depending on the implementation).
Provide many built-in methods.

Array
↓
Fixed Size

Collection
↓
Dynamic Size

====================================================================

Interview Question
Why was the Collection Framework introduced?

Answer:

To overcome the limitations of arrays, such as fixed size and difficult insertion/deletion operations.

## Quick Comparison

## Array | Collection |

Fixed size + high performance | Dynamic size |
Difficult insertion/deletion | Easy insertion/deletion |
Limited utility methods | Rich built-in methods |
Lower flexibility | Higher flexibility |
=============================================================

If an interviewer asks:

Why do arrays still exist if Collections are available?

A strong answer is:

Arrays are faster, use less memory, and are ideal when the number of
elements is fixed. Collections are preferred when the size needs to
change dynamically.

